Z||000003||TRiAD||12-20-2001||09:40 AM||||Hopefully she called the "right" company to do this, and they were properly covered. <P>Their calling it "plum" makes me wonder if it was an anniversary edition...I hope not. Not like "any" Diabo is somehow "OK" to kill. <P>Should have been a robot-made Ferrari, not a handmade Lamborghini.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||12-20-2001||12:03 PM||||How on EARTH do you get 161k in repairs?<BR>Seriously? I just can't fathom it... Are lambo panels and headlights THAT expensive? It does NOT cost 100k to put a car on a frame jig... <P>Triad, you deal in these cars... How the hell does a bender cost 161k to fix!??!||||reg||13
Z||000005||TRiAD||12-20-2001||12:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>...Triad, you deal in these cars... How the hell does a bender cost 161k to fix!??!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, these are not unibody cars, they're on a momocoque chassis, and the panels are mostly carbon fiber, aluminum, and a few fiberglass. <P>The OE paint alone is over $5K per car, and panels generally are not stocked in the US, so they need to be shipped from Italy. <P>It took real craftsmen to make them, and it takes better ones to fix them properly. <P>Anyway, yeah, just like you can "total" any car by doing damage that costs more to fix than it would to replace, this is very possible with most exotics. <P>Remember, a car is worth LESS than the sum of it's parts...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||12-20-2001||01:39 PM||||the Monterey SV that he was driving is one of 200. every panel is vacuum formed kevlar. not carbon fiber cause carbon doesn't flex where kevlar or aramid will with stand a 5mph crash. (DOT Regs) I've contacted the Alfa Romeo, Lotus, Lamborghini Dealer about a Lotus wing. it's nearly $4000. for a wing! the SV wing is an $8000 option. the headlight assemblies are $1800 each and the HID systems I used to sell at NOPI for 900 each. (there are 4 in a Diablo) plus the liability of working on a diablo, the insurance incase some other douche bag does somthing similar in/at the body shop. yeah i could see $160k.  anyone got pics??! ||||reg||1
