Z||000008||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||01:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>When did Britney Spears start working for a towing company?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I dunno but id like to let her tow me somewhere...  Wonder what her "hook up" fee is..  Muuuahhhh hahaha!<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000009||TRiAD||12-20-2001||01:52 PM||||Carbon fiber and Kevlar are formed in an AUTOCLAVE, essentially a HUGE oven/vacuum. <P>The nose on the Diablo is Fiberglass, and is on struts, like ALL bumpers since the 70s. It withstands the 5mph minimun with no damage to the rest of the car. <P>The Diablo has NO kevlar in it. And not all the panels are the same material. The roof is steel, for instance. The bumpers are fiberglass. etc, etc. <P>The headlamp assemblies in the Diablo are the same Stanley units used in the Nissan 300ZX 90-95, and are NOT $1800 ea. They're not even $1800 a pair. Try $250 ea. Add $100ea for the carbon fiber "brow" tacked on at the factory.<P>The Diabo uses ONE HID per side, dims only. The cheap aftermarket units at NOPI (which are now only $600) have NOTHING in common with the $3000 systems in most high-end cars, including the Diablo.<P>The Diablo wing is $6K, not 8. <P>Oh, and they didn't make a Monterey in "plum". Each of the 200 cars was a unique color combination, but no plum.<P>Not a flame, just some correct info. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||12-20-2001||02:02 PM||||Triad... pickey, pickey, pickey.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>None of us will probably ever own a real Diablo (don't think I'd even want to), much less drive one (I know that you broker cars).  So the fine point details are not an issue here, especially not stuff like $6 vs $8 for a wing option. That kind of stuff can vary depending on how much the dealer is going to rape you in the process.<P>The question here is what makes up $161k in repair cost?  Well, think parts cost (extreme due to make), shipping of such parts (Italy), labor (you can't exactly take it to your local collision shop), and paint (expensive no matter if it's called plum or purple- no Maaco here either).  So I can believe an exotic can have that high of a repair bill.||||reg||1
